  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nIn `_decreaseFeeShares` function of `LaunchToken`, it calls `_endRewards` based on a condition `totalFeeShare == 0 && !unlocked`.\n\n`_endRewards` function calls `endRewards` function of `Launchpad` and it calls `endRewards` function of `Distributor`.\n\n- `_endRewards` function of `LaunchToken`\n```solidity\nfunction _endRewards() internal {\n    ILaunchpad(launchpad).endRewards();\n\n    emit FeeShareConcluded(block.timestamp, _incEventNonce());\n}\n```\n\n- `endRewards` function of `Launchpad`\n```solidity\nfunction endRewards() external onlyLaunchAsset {\n    address quote = _launches[msg.sender].quote;\n    // @todo stick with one pair interface\n    IGTELaunchpadV2Pair pair = IGTELaunchpadV2Pair(address(pairFor(address(uniV2Factory), msg.sender, quote)));\n\n    distributor.endRewards(pair);\n}\n```\n\n- `endRewards` function of `Distributor`\n```solidity\nfunction endRewards(IGTELaunchpadV2Pair pair) external onlyLaunchpad {\n    pair.endRewardsAccrual();\n}\n```\nThis condition is totally wrong for the purpose of end rewards that protocol expects to do.\n\nIt should end rewards when bonding curve is finished(means that the token is unlocked) and all bonding curve buyers(users acquired the token through launchpad's buy function) transfered their tokens to others.\n\nBut according to the above condition in `_endRewards` function and working flow, it tries to end rewards process when the `totalFeeShare` is `0` and the token is not unlocked yet.\n\nWhen the token is not unlocked, it means that the token is still in bonding curve and there isn't any pair created by launchpad.\n\nSo there are 2 impacts because of this wrong condition.\n- Firstly, it can't end rewards when it should. (when token is unlocked and all bonding curve buyers transfered their tokens)\n- Secondly, sole buyer(first buyer or last seller while bonding) can't sell his token to launchpad as it tries to call pair's `endRewardsAccrual` function, but the pair is not created yet.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nCall `_endRewards` function based on the correct condition.\n```solidity\nif (totalFeeShare == 0 && unlocked) _endRewards();\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "The first impact is clear as the condition itself shows it.\n\nTo check second impact of this finding, please add below test function to `PoCLaunchpad.t.sol` and run `forge test --mt test_CantBuySellSymmetry -vvvv`.\n\n```solidity\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\n\nfunction test_CantBuySellSymmetry(uint256 amount) public {\n    amount = bound(amount, MIN_BASE_AMOUNT, BONDING_SUPPLY - 1);\n\n    uint256 quote = curve.quoteQuoteForBase(token, amount, true);\n\n    quoteToken.mint(user, quote);\n\n    vm.startPrank(user);\n    launchpad.buy(\n        ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n            account: user,\n            token: token,\n            recipient: user,\n            amountOutBase: amount,\n            maxAmountInQuote: quote\n        })\n    );\n\n    vm.expectRevert();\n    (uint256 baseActual, uint256 quoteActual) = launchpad.sell(user, token, user, amount, quote);\n}\n```",
